---
layout: base.njk
title: AI Citation Tracker
description: Track whether the ASW Hub is cited by Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Microsoft Copilot, and Gemini when answering the five standard ATM queries Maxifi Digital monitors monthly.
permalink: /citation-report/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---

{% set nextDays = citations.summary.firstFullAudit | daysUntil %}

<header class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-monitoring">
      <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Monitoring</span>
      <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
      <span>6 engines · 5 queries · monthly</span>
    </p>
    <h1>AI Citation Tracker</h1>
    <p>Per-engine citation tracking across six AI platforms — Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Microsoft Copilot, and Gemini. Five standard test queries, submitted to each engine monthly. Four of the five target a single post-event canonical record — the SpaceX keynote at the CANSO Leadership Summit 2026 — as the test case for AI pickup of structured hub content.</p>

    <dl class="audit-strip" aria-label="Audit schedule">
      <div>
        <dt>Last audit</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ citations.summary.lastUpdated }}">{{ citations.summary.lastUpdated | longDate }}</time></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Next full audit</dt>
        <dd>
          <time datetime="{{ citations.summary.firstFullAudit }}">{{ citations.summary.firstFullAudit | longDate }}</time>
          {% if nextDays > 0 %}<span class="audit-countdown">in {{ nextDays }} day{% if nextDays != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>{% elif nextDays == 0 %}<span class="audit-countdown">today</span>{% endif %}
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Indexing window</dt>
        <dd>First results June 2026 · Full six-engine audit July 2026</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</header>

<section>
  <div class="container">

    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <div style="background: #f5f5f5; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #555; font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Queries tracked</p>
        <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111;">{{ citations.queries.length }}</p>
        <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #777;">Standard test queries</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #f5f5f5; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #555; font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Engines monitored</p>
        <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111;">{{ citations.engines.length }}</p>
        <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #777;">{% for e in citations.engines %}{{ e.name }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #f5f5f5; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #555; font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">First audit</p>
        <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111;">Jun</p>
        <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #777;">Quick check Jun · Full audit Jul</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="context-strip">
      <aside class="context-card context-card--window">
        <p class="context-label">Indexing window</p>
        <p class="context-body">A new hub takes 4–8 weeks for AI engines to crawl, index, and start citing. Fast movers (Perplexity, Claude) show first; Google AI Overviews, Copilot, and Gemini lag.</p>
      </aside>

      {% if citations.testCase %}
      <aside class="context-card context-card--testcase">
        <p class="context-label">{{ citations.testCase.label }}</p>
        <p class="context-link"><a href="{{ citations.testCase.targetUrl }}">{{ citations.testCase.targetTitle }} →</a></p>
        <p class="context-body">Four of the five queries below target this canonical record of Kiko Dontchev's keynote at the CANSO Leadership Summit, 25 May 2026.</p>
      </aside>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Citation status by standard query</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--paper-faint); margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem;">Each cell shows whether that AI engine cited the hub when answering this query in the latest audit. Green = cited; grey = not yet measured. The <strong>Target</strong> column shows the page each query is designed to surface.</p>

    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.875rem;">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #f5f5f5; border-bottom: 2px solid #e0e0e0; color: #111;">Standard query</th>
            <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem; background: #f5f5f5; border-bottom: 2px solid #e0e0e0; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 0.75rem; color: #111;">Tier</th>
            <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem; background: #f5f5f5; border-bottom: 2px solid #e0e0e0; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 0.75rem; color: #111;">Target page</th>
            {% for engine in citations.engines %}
            <th style="text-align: center; padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem; background: #f5f5f5; border-bottom: 2px solid #e0e0e0; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 0.75rem; color: #111;">{{ engine.name }}</th>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for query in citations.queries %}
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);">
            <td style="padding: 1rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--paper-mute); max-width: 340px;">{{ query.text }}</td>
            <td style="padding: 1rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--paper-mute); white-space: nowrap;">
              {% if query.tier == "Control" %}
                <span style="display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; background: #e5e7eb; color: #374151; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">Control</span>
              {% else %}
                <span style="display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; background: #dbeafe; color: #1d4ed8; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">{{ query.tier }}</span>
              {% endif %}
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 1rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8rem;">
              {% if query.targetUrl %}<a href="{{ query.targetUrl }}" style="color: var(--paper-mute); text-decoration: underline;">{{ query.targetLabel or query.targetUrl }}</a>{% else %}<span style="color: var(--paper-faint);">—</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            {% for engine in citations.engines %}
            {% set engineData = query.engines[engine.id] %}
            <td style="text-align: center; padding: 1rem 0.75rem;">
              {% if engineData and engineData.cited %}
                {% set citedTitle = engineData.quote or ("Hub cited by " + engine.name) %}
                {% if engineData.url %}
                <a href="{{ engineData.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="{{ citedTitle }}" aria-label="Cited by {{ engine.name }}" style="display: inline-block; width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; background: #16a34a; border-radius: 50%; text-align: center; line-height: 1.5rem; color: white; font-size: 0.7rem; text-decoration: none;">✓</a>
                {% else %}
                <span title="{{ citedTitle }}" aria-label="Cited by {{ engine.name }}" style="display: inline-block; width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; background: #16a34a; border-radius: 50%; text-align: center; line-height: 1.5rem; color: white; font-size: 0.7rem;">✓</span>
                {% endif %}
              {% else %}
                <span title="Not yet measured — {{ engine.name }}" aria-label="Not yet measured" style="display: inline-block; width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; border: 2px solid var(--paper-faint); border-radius: 50%; line-height: 1.3rem; text-align: center; color: var(--paper-faint); font-size: 0.85rem;">–</span>
              {% endif %}
            </td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--paper-faint);">✓ = hub cited in latest audit &nbsp;·&nbsp; – = not yet measured &nbsp;·&nbsp; Click ✓ to see the source response</p>

  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions about the tracker</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <h3>What does the AI Citation Tracker measure?</h3>
      <p>It tracks whether the ASW Hub is cited by six AI engines — Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Microsoft Copilot, and Gemini — when answering five standard air traffic management queries that Maxifi Digital submits to each engine monthly. Four of the five queries target a single post-event canonical record (the SpaceX keynote at the CANSO Leadership Summit 2026) as the test case for AI pickup of structured hub content.</p>

      <h3>Which AI engines are monitored?</h3>
      <p>Six: Claude (Anthropic), ChatGPT (OpenAI), Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Microsoft Copilot, and Gemini (Google DeepMind). Each engine is checked against the same five standard queries.</p>

      <h3>How often is the tracker updated?</h3>
      <p>Monthly. The five standard queries are submitted manually to all six engines each month, and the results table updates after each run. First results are expected June 2026, with the full six-engine audit in July 2026.</p>

      <h3>How is a citation recorded?</h3>
      <p>A citation is recorded when an engine either links directly to a page on this hub or quotes its content verbatim in the answer. Until that happens for a given engine and query, the cell is marked as not yet measured.</p>

      <h3>How long does it take for a new hub to be cited by AI engines?</h3>
      <p>A new hub typically takes four to eight weeks for AI engines to crawl, index, and start citing. Fast movers such as Perplexity and Claude tend to show first; Google AI Overviews, Microsoft Copilot, and Gemini usually lag.</p>

      <h3>What is the test case for the tracker?</h3>
      <p>The canonical record of Kiko Dontchev's SpaceX keynote at the CANSO Leadership Summit, held in Lisbon on 25 May 2026. Four of the five standard queries target this single page; query 1 is a generic control query for the whole event.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

