<section class="section-tight" style="border-bottom: 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="maxifi-cta">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
        <h2>How citations are tracked</h2>
        <p>Each month, the five standard queries below are submitted manually to all six engines. Query 1 is a <strong>generic control</strong> — a head-of-funnel browse query for the whole event. Queries 2–5 are <strong>Tier 1 head queries</strong> targeting the SpaceX keynote canonical record, written as a real attendee, journalist, or operator would phrase them after the event. A citation is recorded when an engine either links directly to a page on this hub or quotes its content verbatim in the answer. Results update here after each monthly run. To update: set <code>cited: true</code> and add the source <code>url</code> in <code>src/_data/citations.json</code>, then rebuild.</p>
        <ol style="color: var(--paper-mute); padding-left: 1.4em; margin: 1.25em 0 0; line-height: 1.8;">
          {% for query in citations.queries %}
          <li style="font-size: 0.9rem;">{{ query.text }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="maxifi-cta-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/insights/">All insights →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/how-it-works/">See the methodology</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
